A bug report includes the code shown here:
const raw = '1900';
console.log(parseInt(raw, 10));
Select the two expressions that equal the value printed above.

Check 1901: This short script is part of a small Node utility:
let total = 0;
for (const x of [1901, 2, 3]) { total += x; }
console.log(total);
On this input, what total is printed?

JavaScript interprets this source directly:
const obj = { a: 1902, b: 2 };
let keys = '';
for (const p in obj) { keys += p; }
console.log(keys.length);
From this trace, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

Sample 1903: This example comes from a debugging notebook:
console.log('start');
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log(1903));
console.log('end');
In this run, what is the order of the three logs?

